// This workspace exists to prevent dependency drift across the Token
// Service modules (issuer, auditor, owner, views).
//
// Without it, each module is built with its OWN minimal version selection
// (MVS) run over its OWN go.mod, and Go is free to resolve the SAME
// indirect dependency to DIFFERENT versions in different modules - there
// is nothing forcing them to agree. That exact failure occurred earlier in
// this project: the upstream sample's auditor module resolved
// github.com/consensys/gnark-crypto v0.12.1 while its issuer and owner
// modules resolved v0.18.1, producing an unresolvable linker error against
// github.com/IBM/mathlib (the two gnark-crypto versions are ABI-incompatible
// at that boundary).
//
// Go workspace mode fixes this by computing ONE unified build list across
// every module listed below via `use`, so all four modules are guaranteed
// to select identical versions of every shared indirect dependency
// (github.com/consensys/gnark-crypto, github.com/quic-go/quic-go,
// github.com/libp2p/go-libp2p, etc). This file is the anti-drift mechanism
// for this project and must not be removed. Never build with GOWORK=off.
//
// `views` is included here for the same reason: it is imported by all
// three node modules (see views/logger.go for why it exists), so it must
// share their unified build list too.
//
// go 1.25.7 is the floor imposed by the SDKs themselves: both
// fabric-token-sdk v0.10.1 and fabric-smart-client v0.10.1 declare
// `go 1.25.7` in their go.mod, so this project cannot build on the
// golang:1.24 it used for the previous (v0.3.0) stack.
go 1.25.7

use (
	./auditor
	./issuer
	./owner
	./views
)
